TY  - JOUR
TI  - Utilitarianism does not dominate: a response to Chung
AU  - Shibata, Ryuto
AU  - Wiens, David
PY  - 2025
T2  - Economics and Philosophy
AB  - Chung (2023) purports to derive conditions under which a Utilitarian society, which maximizes total welfare, Pareto dominates a Rawlsian society, which maximizes the income of the least advantaged members of society. We show that Chung’s analysis is doubly flawed. First, his analysis assumes that a Rawlsian government chooses an inefficient tax rate when it could do otherwise. Second, his analysis violates his assumption that citizens must choose a non-negative amount of labour. We show that Chung’s headline result does not hold once we enforce this assumption.
